From: =?UTF-8?q?Lu=C3=ADs=20Duarte?= <lduarte@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:12:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Give outset shadows per-corner radii and corner shapes

Every outset shadow was one analytic rounded rect using the average of
all eight radii, and the spread never grew the radius. A box rounded on
one corner got a shadow rounded on all four, and on shaped corners the
round shadow showed past the cut.

The spread shape now keeps each corner's radii, adjusted by the
css-backgrounds-4 spread formula, and follows corner-shape. Unblurred
shadows fill that exact path. Blurred ones keep the analytic blur,
drawing each quadrant with its own corner's radius, joined on the
straight edges where every radius blurs alike.
